    "sp_qa": {
      "type": "sensol-product-qa",
      "blocks": {
        "qa_1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What makes the FLEX PRO different from the FLEX?",
            "answer": "The FLEX PRO offers three key upgrades: (1) 150 kg max load vs 90 kg — a 33% increase; (2) 0–145° arm range vs 0–132° — the extra 13° unlocks advanced movements and deeper range-of-motion exercises; (3) German steel wire springs vs Spring-based — delivering faster resistance transitions and more consistent tension at high loads. The FLEX PRO is designed for advanced practitioners who need maximum resistance and movement variety."
          }
        },
        "qa_2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What exercises does the 145° arm range unlock?",
            "answer": "The additional 13° of arm range unlocks several categories of exercises impossible on the FLEX or FLEX AIR: deeper lateral flexion patterns targeting the obliques and QL; wider diagonal pull-throughs for rotational core strength; advanced Pilates movements like the full snake, twist, and upward stretch; deeper lunges and split-stance exercises at extreme angles; and wider chest-opening patterns for improved shoulder mobility and thoracic extension."
          }
        },
        "qa_3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is 150 kg max load of resistance too much for Pilates?",
            "answer": "Not at all — that's the beauty of spring resistance increments. For Pilates movements, you'll typically work in the 5–30 kg range, adjusting spring tension to find the exact tension that challenges your form. The 150 kg max load is there for strength training exercises and for the few Pilates practitioners who can genuinely benefit from high-resistance footwork and leg press sequences. The range gives you options; the precision lets you use exactly what you need."
          }
        },
        "qa_4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does the FLEX PRO compare to the Your Reformer?",
            "answer": "The Your Reformer ($2,795) is a spring-based reformer with a wooden frame. The FLEX PRO costs $995 less while offering: 150 kg max load vs ~75 kg; spring resistance vs spring hooks; 3 training modes vs 1; 0–145° adjustable arms vs fixed footbar; dual-function Pilates-plus-strength vs Pilates-only; and precision springs vs audible spring noise. The FLEX PRO is more capable, more versatile, and more technologically advanced."
          }
        },
        "qa_5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can the FLEX PRO replace studio Pilates entirely?",
            "answer": "For most advanced practitioners, yes. The FLEX PRO provides more resistance range than a studio reformer, more exercise variety thanks to the 145° arms and three training modes, and guided programming via the Vesta Sensol App's advanced class library. What it can't replace is the social experience of a group class or the hands-on adjustments of a skilled instructor. But for the actual training, the FLEX PRO delivers an experience that matches or exceeds most studios."
          }
        },
        "qa_6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the Constant Mode, and why is it beneficial?",
            "answer": "Constant Mode maintains perfectly even tension throughout the entire range of motion. On a spring-based reformer, resistance increases as the spring stretches and decreases as it shortens. Constant Mode eliminates this variability, providing consistent resistance from the first centimetre of movement to the last. This is particularly beneficial for rehabilitation, muscle endurance, and muscle growth — where the absence of a 'sticky point' ensures the muscle is challenged throughout the entire movement."
          }
        },
        "qa_7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is the FLEX PRO suitable for rehabilitation?",
            "answer": "Yes. Three features make it ideal: (1) spring resistance increments allow exact resistance matching to a patient's capacity; (2) Constant Mode provides even, controlled tension that eliminates dangerous peak loads; (3) the Vesta Sensol App includes rehabilitation programmes developed with physiotherapy input. Research shows 6–12 weeks of reformer Pilates reduces chronic lower back pain by 30–50%, and the FLEX PRO provides the precision and control needed to achieve these outcomes safely."
          }
        },
        "qa_8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the warranty and return policy?",
            "answer": "The FLEX PRO comes with a Lifetime Warranty on the frame and structural components, plus a 30-Day Money-Back Guarantee. If you're not completely satisfied within 30 days, return it for a full refund. Warranty claims are handled locally in Australia by Dute Fitness (Australia) Pty. Ltd. — no international shipping or long wait times."
          }
        },
        "qa_9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does shipping take? Is it really free?",
            "answer": "Shipping is completely free to all Australian addresses. Standard delivery takes 3–7 business days to metro areas and 5–10 business days to regional areas. Given the 43 kg package weight, free shipping represents $100–$200 in value. You'll receive tracking information via email once your order is dispatched."
          }
        },
        "qa_10": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does the FLEX PRO compare to smart reformers like the NordicTrack Ultra?",
            "answer": "The NordicTrack Ultra costs approximately $17,000+ AUD, requires a $34/month iFIT subscription, and isn't foldable. The FLEX PRO costs $1,800, includes free app access with no subscription, and stores upright in 0.2 m². The FLEX PRO offers more resistance (150 kg max load vs 65 kg), more training modes (3 vs 1), a wider arm range, and dual-function capability. The FLEX PRO delivers essential smart features at a fraction of the price."
          }
        }
      },
